from __future__ import annotations

import json
from pathlib import Path

from author_metadata import load_author_metadata
from build_ijc_submission import repository_statement

PROJECT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
OUT = PROJECT / "manuscript" / "ijc_submission"


def main() -> None:
    data = load_author_metadata()
    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (OUT / "IJC_cover_letter.md").write_text(
        """# Cover Letter\n\nDear Editors,\n\nPlease consider our Research Article, **Estimation-Method Transitions and Cross-Edition Revisions in GLOBOCAN Estimates: A Source-Aware Analysis of 32 Cancers in 185 Countries**, for publication in the *International Journal of Cancer*.\n\nGLOBOCAN releases are widely used for cross-country cancer comparisons, yet differences between releases can reflect changes in estimation inputs and methods as well as changes in reported rates. This study addresses that provenance problem directly. We examine 185 countries or areas, 32 common cancers, 55 applicable cancer-sex combinations, and 20,350 paired incidence and mortality cells from GLOBOCAN 2022 and 2024. Two blinded human reviewers classified all 370 source-method pairs, a third author adjudicated escalations, and the final exposure was analysed with parsimonious robust country-level models, region-stratified bootstrap inference, falsification analyses, and external registry-capacity checks.\n\nThe principal contribution is methodological: the analysis separates administrative or wording changes from substantive changes in directness and reports the uncertainty of that semantic classification. The adjusted differences were +1.468 percentage points for incidence and -0.786 percentage points for mortality, with intervals crossing zero in both analyses. We therefore avoid treating either release as a gold standard or interpreting the edition difference as a simple temporal trend.\n\nThe work is complementary to recent IJC studies of cross-release stability and genitourinary estimate consistency (DOIs: 10.1002/ijc.70773 and 10.1002/ijc.70719), while extending the comparison to source-method provenance across a broader cancer and country set. The manuscript is original, is not under consideration elsewhere, and all authors have approved its submission.\n\n""" + repository_statement() + "\n\nSincerely,\n\nHui Zhang\nThe First Clinical College, Changsha Medical University\n515009366@qq.com\nORCID: 0000-0003-4513-5606\n""",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )
    (OUT / "IJC_figure_table_legends.md").write_text(
        """# Figure and Table Legends\n\n**Figure 1. Source-method transition structure after human adjudication.** Panel A shows counts and percentages for the five final adjudication categories within each indicator; the denominator is 185 country-indicator pairs per indicator. Panels B and C show 2022-to-2024 directness transition matrices. Directness is a provenance descriptor, not a data-quality or accuracy ranking.\n\n**Figure 2. Country-level revision magnitude and substantive source-method transition.** Each point is one country with a complete primary-model covariate set. Panels A and B show incidence and mortality against baseline median ASR. Colours identify substantive transition status; open squares are group medians. LOWESS curves use the pinned reference grammar (f=0.6, iter=3) and are drawn only over the group-specific 5th-95th percentile of the observed x range. The inset reports the adjusted marginal difference, region-stratified bootstrap 95% CI, and permutation P value. Curves are descriptive; inference is from the adjusted model.\n\n**Figure 3. Cancer-specific revision magnitude by adjudicated source-method exposure.** Tiles report median ASPD after the ASR2022 >0.5 per 100,000 floor for administrative/wording-only and substantive-transition strata. Cancers use one pooled descending order across panels. Colours saturate at 60%; exact values are printed in cells. NA denotes a structural absence, not zero.\n\n**Figure 4. External convergent checks.** Panel A shows incidence ASPD by WHO population-based cancer registry existence. Panel B shows mortality ASPD against WHO cause-of-death completeness. Points are countries and open squares are group summaries. The LOWESS curve uses f=0.6 and iter=3. These indicators are convergent checks, not independent truth labels.\n\n**Table 1.** Country-indicator characteristics by final adjudicated source-method category.\n\n**Table 2.** Final-exposure model coefficients, diagnostics, marginal effects, and bootstrap stability.\n\n**Supplementary Figure S1.** Bland-Altman agreement between GLOBOCAN 2022 and 2024 ASRs.\n""",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )
    (OUT / "IJC_supplementary_material.md").write_text(
        """# Supplementary Material\n\n## Supplementary Figure\n\nSupplementary Figure S1 presents Bland-Altman summaries for paired ASRs with ASR2022 >0.1.\n\n## Supplementary Tables\n\nSupplementary Table S1: final adjudicated category counts.\n\nSupplementary Table S2: country-level final exposure and model covariates.\n\nSupplementary Table S3: ASR-floor sensitivity analyses.\n\nSupplementary Table S4: UNCLASSIFIABLE boundary analysis.\n\nSupplementary Table S5: leave-one-region-out analyses.\n\nSupplementary Table S6: external convergent checks and key sensitivity analyses, including death-registration coverage.\n\nSupplementary Table S7: cancer-specific estimates and FDR-adjusted results.\n\n## Supplementary Methods\n\nThe supplement contains the source-method codebook, AI input/output sealing manifest, anonymized agreement summary, directness mapping, adjudication process, missing-data definitions, all alternative outcome definitions, full model diagnostics, and the complete figure source-data tables. Restricted row-level reviewer files and country keys are retained in the private research record and are not included in the public or submission package.\n""",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )
    (OUT / "IJC_STROBE_RECORD_checklist.md").write_text(
        """# STROBE and RECORD Checklist\n\n| Item | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Study design | Addressed | Ecological secondary-data comparison described in Materials and Methods |\n| Setting and data sources | Addressed | GLOBOCAN 2022/2024, WHO GHO and UNDP HDI sources identified |\n| Participants/units | Addressed | 185 countries, 370 source-method pairs, 55 cancer-sex combinations and 20,350 paired cells |\n| Variables | Addressed | ASPD, source-method exposure, directness, HDI and external indicators defined |\n| Bias | Addressed | Blinding, adjudication, sparse exposure, ecological and coverage limitations reported |\n| Study size | Addressed | Complete paired design and exclusions reported |\n| Quantitative variables | Addressed | ASR floor, ASPD formula, log-ratio and threshold outcomes specified |\n| Statistical methods | Addressed | HC3 regression, GEE, region-stratified bootstrap, permutation and FDR described |\n| Missing data | Addressed | HDI and external indicators are complete-case with coverage reported; no silent imputation |\n| Sensitivity analyses | Addressed | ASR floors, source restrictions, influence and leave-one-region-out analyses reported |\n| Results precision | Addressed | Confidence intervals, bootstrap success and diagnostics reported |\n| Limitations | Addressed | No gold standard, ecological design, metadata granularity and reference-year differences discussed |\n| Data access | Addressed | Public release plan, retrieval instructions and exclusion of restricted/raw files stated |\n| RECORD applicability | Addressed | Study uses routinely available aggregate secondary data; relevant RECORD items are described in the supplement |\n| Ethics | Not applicable | No identifiable human data |\n| Registration/protocol | Not applicable | Result-aware SAP v2 is identified as an amendment, not prospective registration |\n""",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )
    (OUT / "PUBLIC_RELEASE_INSTRUCTIONS.md").write_text(
        """# Public Release Handoff\n\n1. Create a public GitHub repository named `globocan-source-method-transitions`.\n2. Upload only the files in the generated public-release staging directory; do not upload the private project directory.\n3. Confirm that bulk GCO files, Wiley PDFs, country keys, reviewer-level ratings, adjudication rationales, local paths and logs are absent.\n4. Create the GitHub release tag `v1.0.0-submission`.\n5. Enable the GitHub-Zenodo integration and archive that exact tag.\n6. Record the Zenodo DOI and release URL in `config/journal_profile.yml` and the manuscript data-availability statement.\n7. Re-run `python scripts/ijc_integrity.py`. The submission gate remains false until the DOI is present and both ZIP privacy scans pass.\n\nThe corresponding author must perform the authenticated GitHub and Zenodo actions. No credentials are stored in the project.\n""",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )
    print(json.dumps({"output": str(OUT), "corresponding_author": "Hui Zhang"}, indent=2))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
